## Additional Packages Detected
The project also has `@vercel/speed-insights` (version 2.0.0) properly configured alongside Analytics, providing comprehensive performance and analytics tracking.

## Next Steps for Project Owner
1. **Enable Analytics in Vercel Dashboard**: Navigate to your project's Analytics section in the Vercel dashboard and click "Enable" if not already done
2. **Deploy**: Push changes to trigger a Vercel deployment (though no code changes were needed)
3. **Verify**: After deployment, check browser Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*` endpoints
4. **View Data**: Access analytics data through the Vercel dashboard once users visit your site

## Conclusion
No code changes were required. The project already has Vercel Web Analytics correctly installed and configured according to the latest official documentation. The implementation is production-ready and will start collecting analytics data once enabled in the Vercel dashboard and deployed.
